  clock: 3  # f8fb
  nonce: f8fb  # f8fb
  message: "DONE in PR #2326 (dev 92cd212a6). DECISION (the item left it open, withhold or label): both. An unreached callable is reported only where the run holds a call-family edge (calls or instantiates) onto some in-repo callable of its language and kind. The unreached callables of a (language, kind) group with no such edge are withheld from dead_candidates and dead_percent, counted in summary.withheld_no_call_evidence, and listed in no_call_evidence_withheld with their groups in no_call_evidence_groups; both lists are always present, and the text view prints the count always. DEAD_CODE_MAYBE_SCHEMA_VERSION 0.3.0 to 0.4.0, additive. It is a rule, not a list of languages. This is the treatment the view already gives its cross-language demoter. If the owner wants only one of the two, it is a small change.\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (2026-11-22, hypergumbo dead-code-maybe over one map, dev code vs fixed code): a fixture with SQL, CMake and SCSS functions (three analyzers that emit function nodes and no calls edge, confirmed in the map) and three Python functions: 7 of 10 reported dead on dev, 0 after, 7 withheld in three groups; under --seeds entrypoints the Python orphan is still reported. mastodon sub-tree 84 to 82 (5 JavaScript methods withheld: no call edge lands on any JavaScript method in that run). pretix src/pretix 7,660 to 7,657 (6 SCSS functions withheld). 10 of 10 mutations red.\nTHE FILED SIGHTINGS (Verilog 13 of 13, F# 7 to 48) were not re-run: both analyzers were given call edges before they merged, so those fixtures no longer show the defect.\nTHE COUNT THE ITEM SAID WAS NOT DONE: by grep, 12 of 120 analyzer modules mention a function or method kind and never the string calls: proto, qml, rst, scss, thrift, capnp, gnuplot, twig, cmake, make, play_routes, sql. Confirmed by a run for sql, cmake, scss only.\nLIMITS: one edge clears its whole group, so a weak instrument is not graded (filed). Withheld candidates no longer reach the cross-language demoter (its count fell by 3 on each of the two repos). test-coverage reads no-test-reaches-it the same way and was not examined (filed).\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/three_pr_plan_11222026/pr1/RESULTS.md."  # f8fb
